    },
    {
      "fragment_type": "constraint_statement",
      "content": "Overall risk-benefit analysis conclusion: The risk management process of this design change is based on the application standards of risk management for medical devices, and combines product characteristics and corresponding regulatory requirements. The risk management team considered all regulatory requirements that affect product performance and safety, and did not generate new risks or affect existing risks, so it is believed that the overall benefits outweigh the risks. After reviewing the design changes of the PT2L infrared thermometer product, the risk management team believes that: (1) This design change has been properly implemented according to the risk management plan; (2) Combined with the overall risk-benefit analysis, the comprehensive residual risk of this design change is acceptable.",
      "topic_tags": [
